I just though of a different compensation for the cold iron
restriction: cold iron affects elves as I described, but physical
damage from other sources (e.g. non-iron weapons, natural attacks,
etc.) would be healed at the rate of 1 hp/round, as if the elf were
wearing a ring of regeneration.  This would only be physical damage,
and wouldn't include spells, fire, electricity, etc.  This would be
somewhat of a pain to implement, though.

Another approach: contact with cold iron does not harm elves, and cold
iron weapons do a normal amount of damage, but damage done by iron
does not heal naturally.  The elf must heal via a spell, potion, or
other healing effect other than just time.  Maybe combine this with
the physical damage regeneration I described above to balance it out.

